# Frontend configuration.
#
# NEVER put a secret in a VITE_ variable. Vite inlines them into the published
# bundle at build time, so a VITE_-prefixed secret is a published secret
# (ADR-017, ADR-018). GROQ_API_KEY, RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET and
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET belong to the backend and must never appear here.
# The only credential that reaches the browser is the *public* Razorpay key id,
# and it arrives in a response body at checkout time, not from configuration.

# Where the backend is. Must match an entry in the backend's
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, or every request fails in the browser only.
#
# NOTE: port 8000 is the natural default, but another application may already be
# using it on this machine. If the health panel reports a malformed response,
# check what is actually listening on 8000 before debugging anything else.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
